cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. It is unrefereed and was produced largely with AI assistance (see README.md)."
title: "A certified simple, even ground state of the localized Weil quadratic form for all windows L in (0, 2]"
abstract: "Computer-assisted proof, in Arb ball arithmetic and exact integer arithmetic, that the lowest eigenvalue of the localized Weil quadratic form for the Riemann zeta function on L^2(-L, L) is simple with an even eigenfunction for every L in (0, 2]. Pieces I-II cover (0, 1.19]; Piece III covers [1.19, 1.4035] with second-eigenvalue lower bounds from Elston's certifier plus a rank-one deflation; Piece IV (new in 2.0.0) covers [1.4035, 2] with a clean-room implementation of the rh_60-route full-source Schur certificate (method of bramble_trace and lihongmin, unrefereed AI-agent preprints) extended by a rank-one deflation and an exact-integer structured LDL (Lemma SR), on a pre-registered grid of 54 windows. The registered grid failed at one window; the gap is closed by a post-hoc, pre-stamped rule (rule E) and, without that rule, by min-max monotonicity from a registered certificate at the next window. Upper bounds are rigorous Legendre-Galerkin Rayleigh quotients. Not a result about the Riemann hypothesis. Unrefereed; produced largely with AI assistance and audited only by AI agents."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Johann Alexander"
    family-names: "Botha"
    email: "info@genuscore.com"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
